<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korea's Jan-Feb energy demand up 1.9 pct.</title>
<headline>South Korea's Jan-Feb energy demand up 1.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's energy demand rose 1.9 percent to 30.04 million tonnes of oil equivalent (TOE) in the first two months compared to a year ago, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Consumption growth of oil products dragged in the first two months of this year due to slower demand from industrial, home and commercial sectors, a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>But demand for liquefied natural gas (LNG) surged on the back of increasing use for power generation.</p>
<p>Breakdown of South Korea's demand for energy resources in January to February, compared with the same period last year (Figures in brackets are year-on-year growth in percentage):</p>
<p>				Jan-Feb 1997	  Jan-Feb 1996</p>
<p>				Amount		  Amount</p>
<p> Total			30,043   (1.9)	29,490  (10.3)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE)</p>
<p> Petroleum products    136,477   (0.5)     135,862   (6.6)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 barrels)</p>
<p> LNG			   2,546  (37.1)	 1,857  (30.0)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Hard coal		     619 (-22.2)	   796 (-15.3)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Bituminous coal	   6,772  (-5.6)	 7,175  (23.7)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Nuclear power	    11,104  (-2.7)	11,412   (7.0)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Hydroelectric power	 685  (-4.7)	   719  (18.2)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Other			   202  (14.1)	   177   (6.5)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE)</p>
<p>(Source: Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy).</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
